---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const chapters = (await getCollection('chapters', ({ data }) => data.language === 'en')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order
);
const nodes = await getCollection('argument-nodes');
const sources = await getCollection('sources');
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  lang={lang}
  description="Interactive Christian Inquiry Project — Phase 0 prototype. Deeper questions, not slogans."
>
  <h1>CREDO The Inquiry</h1>
  <p
    style="font-family: var(--font-sans); color: var(--color-ink-soft); font-size: var(--fs-small); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 var(--gap-2) 0;"
  >
    Phase 0 prototype — mobile-first, source-grounded, logically disciplined
  </p>

  <p>
    An interactive knowledge system for tracing a chain of questions: the problem of evil → divine
    foreknowledge → causation → freedom → permission → suffering → theism → revelation → Jesus → resurrection
    → apostles → Scripture → Tradition → Church → authority → Catholic claim.
  </p>

  <p>
    The project is not merely an apologetics article collection. Its core asset is the structured argument and
    source graph behind the presentation. Visualizations explain reasoning. Worldviews are not given numerical
    scores.
  </p>

  <h2>Start here</h2>
  <ul>
    {
      chapters.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <strong>Chapter {c.data.order}:</strong>{' '}
          <a href={`${base}/en/chapters/${c.data.chapter_slug}`}>{c.data.title}</a>
          <div style="font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--color-ink-soft);">
            {c.data.nodes_used.length} argument nodes · {c.data.sources_used.length} sources
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Counts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${base}/en/nodes`}>{nodes.length} argument nodes</a> (POE-001 through POE-015)</li>
    <li>
      <a href={`${base}/en/sources`}>{sources.length} source records</a> (CCC, primary philosophy, patristic, reference)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Non-negotiable rules</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>No invented quotations, sources, page numbers, or Catholic doctrine.</li>
    <li>Textual claims are kept separate from theological claims.</li>
    <li>Conclusions are bounded by premises.</li>
    <li>
      Foreknowledge, causation, permission, intention, possibility, plausibility, defense, and theodicy remain
      distinct.
    </li>
    <li>Plantinga's Free Will Defense is presented as a defense, not as a complete solution.</li>
    <li>Fallen angels are not invoked to explain particular natural disasters.</li>
    <li>Not every natural evil is mapped to a particular sin.</li>
    <li>Catholicism is not declared established before the relevant arguments are developed.</li>
    <li>No arbitrary numerical scores for worldviews.</li>
  </ol>
</Layout>
